    <DataNode elementId="AT5G16760-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G16760-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SBA5" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;AT5g16760&lt;/i&gt; encodes a protein with Ins(1,3,4) 5-/6-kinase activity. AtIpk1 was recombinantly expressed in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; and purified to test its substrate specificity. The enzyme was shown to use Ins(1,3,4)P&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt; as a substrate to produce Ins(1,3,4,5)P&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; and Ins(1,3,4,6)P&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; in a 3:1 ratio |CITS:[9126335]|. No evidence of the phosphorylation of Ins(1,4,5)P&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;, Ins(1,4)P&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;, Ins(1)P, Ins(2)P, Ins(3)P or cyclic Ins(1,2)P by the recombinant protein was found |CITS:[9126335]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G16760-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G16760.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Swissmodel" value="Q9SBA5" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Modbase" value="Q9SBA5" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR14217" />
